UID:10009522-1788636600-1788645600@unitedarts.org
SUMMARY:Once Upon a One More Time
DESCRIPTION:Powered by the chart-topping hits of the undisputed Princess of Pop\, Once Upon A One More Time turns our favorite fairytales upside down with a clever twist! When a fairy godmother goes rogue and plops copies of The Feminine Mystique in the laps of classic heroines\, the damsels embark on a quest to rewrite their stories and redefine “happily ever after.”  \nPerformed by Theatre Raleigh ACT Performance Company students
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/once-upon-a-one-more-time/2026-09-05/
LOCATION:De Ann S. Jones Theatre at Theatre Raleigh Arts Center\, 6638 Old Wake Forest Road\, Raleigh
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/onceuponaobemoretime.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Theatre Raleigh":MAILTO:info@theatreraleigh.com
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:United Arts Wake County
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T220000
DTSTAMP:20260727T180817Z
CREATED:20260727T180817Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260727T180817Z
UID:10010117-1788636600-1788645600@unitedarts.org
SUMMARY:Hairspray
DESCRIPTION:It’s 1962 in Baltimore\, and the lovable plus-size teen\, Tracy Turnblad\, has only one desire – to dance on the popular “Corny Collins Show.” When her dream comes true\, Tracy is transformed from social outcast to sudden star. She must use her newfound power to dethrone the reigning Teen Queen\, win the affections of heartthrob\, Link Larkin\, and integrate a TV network… all without denting her ‘do! Hairspray\, winner of eight Tony Awards\, including Best Musical\, is a family-friendly musical\, piled bouffant-high with laughter\, romance and deliriously tuneful songs. \nBook by Mark O’Donnell & Thomas Meehan \nMusic by Marc Shaiman \nLyrics by Scott Wittman & Marc Shaiman \nBased on the New Line Cinema film\, written and directed by John Waters
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/hairspray/2026-09-05/
LOCATION:Raleigh Little Theatre\, 301 Pogue St\, Raleigh\, 27607
ORGANIZER;CN="Raleigh Little Theatre":MAILTO:boxoffice@raleighlittletheatre.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:United Arts Wake County
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T223000
DTSTAMP:20260610T175909Z
CREATED:20260610T175909Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260610T175909Z
UID:10008750-1788636600-1788647400@unitedarts.org
SUMMARY:The Hunchback of Notre Dame
DESCRIPTION:The sweeping\, epic musical based on Victor Hugo’s timeless tale and the beloved Disney film comes to life like never before! Featuring a soaring score by Alan Menken and Stephen Schwartz\, this powerful story of love\, acceptance\, and courage will be performed in the hauntingly beautiful Vintage Church in Downtown Raleigh. In partnership with the North Carolina Master Chorale\, Theatre Raleigh is creating the expansive choir needed for this majestic\, site-specific theatrical experience—truly unforgettable from start to finish.
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/the-hunchback-of-notre-dame/2026-09-05/
LOCATION:Vintage Church on Moore Square in Downtown Raleigh  118 S Person St\, Raleigh\, NC 27601\, 118 S Person St\, Raleigh\, 27601
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/hunchbacksquare.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Theatre Raleigh":MAILTO:info@theatreraleigh.com
END:VEVENT
